  <info>
    <language>en-IN</language>
    <category>Met</category>
    <event>Cyclone Warning</event>
    <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
    <severity>Extreme</severity>
    <certainty>Observed</certainty>
    <senderName>India Meteorological Department</senderName>
    <headline>Severe Cyclonic Storm to cross Odisha coast near Gopalpur</headline>
    <description>
      A Severe Cyclonic Storm over the west-central Bay of Bengal is very likely
      to cross the Odisha coast between Gopalpur and Chatrapur during the next
      12 hours, with sustained wind speeds of 110-120 kmph gusting to 135 kmph,
      a storm surge of 1.5-2.0 m above astronomical tide, and extremely heavy
      rainfall over Ganjam district.
    </description>
    <instruction>
      Move to the nearest designated cyclone shelter. Do not cross flowing
      water. Fishermen are advised not to venture into the sea. Keep mobile
      phones charged and follow instructions from the District Administration.
    </instruction>
